  "body": "**What happened (2026-11-12).** A contributor with label rights ran the review skill on their own PRs (#560, #1131, #1136, #1156): their account posted comments whose first line is `<!-- pr-reviewer: <head sha> -->` and set `merge-ready`. Our tooling then treated those heads as reviewed:\n- `/review-prs` step 1 selects PRs with no comment or review containing the marker for the current head - it does not look at who wrote it, so three PRs that never had an independent review dropped out of the queue;\n- `/merge-ready` (step 1, \"head moved since the review\") and `/resolve-conflicts check` (restore `merge-ready` when the head is unchanged) read the same marker and label;\n- on #560 `merge-ready` sat beside our own `needs-rework`.\n\n**Decision (maintainer, question dialog, 2026-11-12):** \"No, only ours count\" - a review counts only when the maintainer's account posted it; a contributor does not mark or label their own PRs as reviewed.\n\n**To do.**\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`: the step-1 query and every other marker read count only markers authored by the repository owner's account (`gh repo view --json owner`), in both `reviews` and `comments`; same for the `review-cost` marker.\n- `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/` (maintainer mode) and `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`: same rule where they read an earlier review.\n- Each `/review-prs` run: a `merge-ready` label last set by an account other than the owner's, with no owner-authored marker for the current head, is removed with a one-line comment (labels come from `repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/N/events`).\n- AGENTS.md \"Outside PRs are reviewed\": one sentence stating the rule, and that a contributor's own pre-check is a plain comment without the marker.\n- Bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`; announce on #681.\n- The local `merge-ready` skill (not in the repo) needs the same author check; the maintainer's session does that.\n\nDone means: a PR whose only marker for its current head was written by another account is listed by `/review-prs` as needing review and is never offered by `/merge-ready`; pinned by the skill text and, where the query lives in a script, by a test.\n",
